[2026-06-03 21:38:43] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"66b46c66-8db9-4176-86bd-12395acb3f94","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\66b46c66-8db9-4176-86bd-12395acb3f94.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"default","agent_id":"a54054afd34ce9d0c","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\66b46c66-8db9-4176-86bd-12395acb3f94\\subagents\\agent-a54054afd34ce9d0c.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"I have now thoroughly explored the backend API directory and read all files completely. Here's a comprehensive summary of the backend API structure:\n\n## Backend API Directory Structure\n\n### API Layer (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\api\\`)\n\n**1. config_handler.go**\n- Handles system configuration management (GET/PUT /api/config)\n- Supports partial updates via JSON map\n- Validates configuration keys and values\n\n**2. health_handler.go**\n- Simple health check endpoint (/health)\n- Returns {status: \"ok\"}\n\n**3. issue_handler.go**\n- Issue management endpoints:\n  - POST /api/issue/check - Check issue status\n  - POST /api/issue/claim - Claim an issue\n  - POST /api/issue/release - Release a single issue\n  - POST /api/issue/release-session - Release all issues for a session\n  - POST /api/issue/status - Update issue status\n  - GET /api/issues - List issues with filtering and pagination\n\n**4. log_handler.go**\n- Query backend service logs (/api/logs)\n- Supports filtering by level, date, and limit\n\n**5. machine_handler.go**\n- List machines with filtering by OS and hostname (/api/machines)\n\n**6. project_handler.go**\n- List all projects (/api/projects)\n\n**7. proxy_handler.go**\n- Proxy management:\n  - POST /api/proxy/register - Register proxy\n  - POST /api/proxy/unregister - Unregister proxy\n  - POST /api/proxy/trace-init - Forward trace-init requests\n  - GET /api/proxies - List proxies\n\n**8. request.go**\n- Defines all request structures for API endpoints\n\n**9. response.go**\n- Defines all response structures and helper functions (writeJSON, writeError)\n\n**10. router.go**\n- Central route registration using HTTP multiplexer\n- Wires all handlers to their respective endpoints\n\n**11. session_handler.go**\n- Session management:\n  - POST /api/session/register - Register new session\n  - POST /api/session/close - Close session\n  - GET /api/sessions - List sessions\n  - GET /api/session/{id} - Get session details\n  - GET /api/session/{id}/issues - Get session's issues\n  - GET /api/session/{id}/tokens - Get token statistics\n  - GET /api/session/{id}/traces - Get trace files\n\n**12. status_handler.go**\n- System status endpoint (/api/status)\n- Returns system health, version, uptime, and statistics\n\n### Service Layer (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\service\\`)\n\n**1. cleanup_service.go**\n- Cleans up timed-out sessions (older than 24 hours)\n\n**2. config_service.go**\n- System configuration business logic\n\n**3. idle_watchdog.go**\n- Monitors proxy.json for idle periods\n- Triggers graceful shutdown after 10 minutes of inactivity\n\n**4. issue_service.go**\n- Issue management business logic\n- Handles claiming, releasing, status updates, and listing\n\n**5. log_service.go**\n- Log parsing and querying functionality\n- Supports filtering by level and date\n\n**6. machine_service.go**\n- Machine listing and retrieval\n\n**7. project_service.go**\n- Project listing and retrieval\n\n**8. proxy_service.go**\n- Proxy listing with filtering\n\n**9. session_service.go**\n- Session registration, closing, listing, and retrieval\n\n**10. status_service.go**\n- System statistics aggregation\n- Counts active sessions, proxies, pending issues, etc.\n\n**11. token_service.go**\n- Token usage statistics by parsing trace files\n- Calculates totals for API calls, input/output tokens, cache usage\n\n**12. trace_service.go**\n- Trace file metadata extraction\n- Calculates file size and line counts\n\n### Store Layer (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\store\\`)\n\n**1. config_store.go**\n- SQLite implementation for system configuration\n- Supports key-value storage with validation\n\n**2. issue_store.go**\n- Issue persistence with optimistic locking\n- Auto-creates idle records for new issues\n- Supports claims, status updates, and releases\n\n**3. machine_store.go**\n- Machine data persistence\n\n**4. migrations.go**\n- Database schema creation\n- Tables for: machines, projects, sessions, issue_claims, config, proxies\n\n**5. project_store.go**\n- Project data persistence\n\n**6. proxy_store.go**\n- Proxy registration data persistence\n\n**7. session_store.go**\n- Session registration with transactional updates to machines and projects\n- Handles session closure and cleanup\n\n**8. sqlite.go**\n- SQLite store initialization and connection management\n- Enables WAL mode for better concurrency\n\n**9. store.go**\n- Domain interfaces and types\n- Common error definitions\n\n### Domain Layer (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\domain\\`)\n\n**1. issue.go**\n- Issue status enumeration (idle, claimed, fixing, ready-for-pr, etc.)\n- IssueClaim entity definition\n\n**2. machine.go**\n- Machine entity definition\n\n**3. project.go**\n- Project entity definition\n\n**4. session.go**\n- Session status enumeration (active, closed)\n- Session entity definition\n\n**5. token.go**\n- Token statistics structure with calculation methods\n\n### Server Integration (`D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\claude_tap_plus\\internal\\backend\\server.go`)\n\n- Main server initialization and startup\n- Service layer instantiation\n- Route registration via api.NewRouter\n- Graceful shutdown with signal handling\n- Idle watchdog integration\n\n## Key Features\n\n1. **Issue Management**: Full CRUD operations with optimistic locking and state machine\n2. **Session Management**: Tracks Claude Code sessions with metadata\n3. **Proxy Support**: Dynamic proxy registration and trace-init forwarding\n4. **Monitoring**: Health checks, system statistics, and log querying\n5. **Configuration Runtime**: Dynamic system configuration updates\n6. **Auto-cleanup**: Automatic session timeout cleanup and idle shutdown\n7. **Pagination**: Supports paginated listing for issues and sessions\n8. **Filtering**: Rich filtering options across all entities\n9. **Transaction Safety**: Database operations use transactions where appropriate\n\nThe backend follows a clean architecture with clear separation between API (HTTP), Service (business logic), and Store (persistence) layers, making it maintainable and testable.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
